R CMD INSTALL: compile preflight (rzig's check mode names what is missing)

A package needs the toolchain when it has compiled code (src/) or a
configure script R runs: configure, or on Windows configure.ucrt or
configure.win (there R does not run a plain configure, it only warns).
rzig, R_HOME/bin/toolchain/zig-cc (gcc.exe on Windows), finds each
toolchain group's tools as a compile does, on every channel: its check
mode `--rzig-check=package` (check.zig) decides for the package in the
working directory, as `rzig build` (patch 0013, feat-zig-pkg-build)
decides in run_shlib, through one function (pkgbuild.decide: the
files, then the Makevars and Makeconf), whether it builds through zig
build alone (tiers 0-2) or needs make (tier 3), and checks the groups
that build needs: the compilers, flang when Fortran is compiled (with a
configure script R runs, src/'s top level, either case of the f,
whatever the tier; otherwise the plan's sources for tier 1, never for
tier 2, whose src/build.zig compiles C and C++ only, and src/'s top
level for a package make builds, as R's default OBJECTS rule compiles
them: Fortran a Makevars builds from a subdirectory stops later, at
zig-fc, with the same text [preflight-PF-5]), and the build tools when
the package needs make or R runs a configure script (R_ZIG_CONFIGURE=1),
whatever its tier. A check that fails exits non-zero after a line
saying what is missing, with rzig's own reason when make is needed
("<pkg> needs make: src/Makevars has a rule or target line: '...'; no
make on PATH"), and the group's text, which names how to install it
(each missing group's, in one stop: PHASE4 open point H a); a
src/build.zig package whose build would need make, which ignores
build.zig, fails with "<pkg>: src/build.zig cannot be built by make:
<reason>" [preflight-PF-1] and "<pkg>: the r-zig toolchain is complete:
change what the line above names" [code-6]. Run it before the configure
step and stop with that text, instead of failing deep in configure or
make. rzig ships with R on every channel (the base archive,
r-zig-slim, the r-zig wheel; feat-standalone-toolchain phase 4). A
check that exits 127 (a group missing) stops with "this package needs
the r-zig toolchain (compiled code or a configure script), which is
incomplete (see above)", after a user's own R_ZIG_TOOLCHAIN_HINT as a
"hint:" line when one is set: an R-only package with a configure
script stops too [tests-T11]. Any other status (a package make cannot
build, a zig that is not R's, a path that does not resolve) stops with
"this package cannot be built (see above)" (PHASE4 open point J a). The
C standard (use_C, the hook's --c-std) goes through R_ZIG_C_STD;
R_ZIG_PKG_BUILDER=make makes the check ask for the build tools. A user
Makevars (their own compiler) or R_ZIG_NO_PREFLIGHT skips the check;
binary packages never reach it. Four inputs differ from the hook's, and
are recorded: CLINK_CPPFLAGS is set only after the preflight, the
user-Makevars skip stays, and use_LTO and Windows' --debug are not
passed [preflight-PF-7].
feat-no-host-paths PLAN.md, phase T; feat-standalone-toolchain PLAN.md,
B26, B35 and phase 4; feat-zig-pkg-build PLAN.md, consolidation M1.

